# DevKit Design Constitution (Agent Rule)

Single source of truth for visual, interaction, responsive, a11y, motion, spacing, type, color, radius, elevation, material, density, and layout:

→ `.cursor/rules/design-main-rule.mdc` (sections **01–100**)

Short always-on summary: `.cursor/rule/design-rule.md`

## Enforce on every UI change

1. Use constitution tokens only — never invent spacing, colors, type, radius, motion, or control sizes.
2. Spatial system: **4px base / 8px rhythm** (`space-0`…`space-64`).
3. One adaptive component across Compact→Ultra Wide breakpoints — no per-breakpoint forks.
4. Semantic colors; Light / Dark / High Contrast as independent themes.
5. **No box-shadows and no gradients** — elevation via surface tone + border.
6. **DevKit scrollbars** — use `--scrollbar-*` tokens / `.dk-scroll*`; never leave browser-default chrome.
7. Visible focus, ≥44×44 touch targets, never color-only status, honor reduced motion.
8. Do not duplicate global foundation rules inside component prompts — only uniqueness (§99–100).
9. Optical refinement pass before done (§94): alignment, baseline, padding symmetry, contrast, timing, touch, focus.

Target feel: calm + premium + precise + fluid + intelligent + beautiful + highly usable — without copying Apple proprietary UI.
